## Drop extra Generate subClassOf parents (single inheritance)
================================================================================

Context:
Ontology → Generate on an existing ontology could propose a second
rdfs:subClassOf parent for a class that already inherits. The OntoBricks
model stores a single `parent` per class, so the extra axiom either failed
merge or could not be represented. Generate now refuses extra parents:
locked anchors snapshot the existing parent, the axioms prompt forbids a
second one, parsing drops extras, and merge keeps the live parent.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/ontology/generate/GenerateDraft.py
   Snapshot `parent` on locked anchors; expose `existing_parents()`.
2. src/agents/agent_owl_generator/prompts.py
   List existing subclass axioms; require single inheritance.
3. src/agents/agent_owl_generator/schemas.py
   Drop extra `subClassOf` parents in `parse_axioms_payload`.
4. src/agents/agent_owl_generator/staged.py
   Pass existing parents into axiom parsing.
5. src/back/objects/ontology/generate/GenerateWorkflow.py
   Merge keeps the existing parent and ignores extra `subClassOf` axioms.
6. src/agents/agent_owl_generator/engine.py
   Legacy OWL guidelines: one superclass only.
7. src/agents/PITFALL_RULES.md
   P4.2: do not assign a second superclass.
8. tests/eval/datasets/agent_owl_generator/baseline.jsonl
   Rows `staged-single-inheritance-001..003`; floor 28 → 31.

