## Classify SEA-wrapped VIEW errors; keep Apps bearer on Playwright continue
================================================================================

Context: Live campaign scenario 5 failed after a successful Lakehouse
zero-copy build because ``DESCRIBE DETAIL`` on the ``…_data`` VIEW comes
back from Statement Execution as ``InfrastructureError("Databricks SQL
statement failed")`` with ``EXPECT_TABLE_NOT_VIEW`` only in ``detail``.
Classifiers that look at ``str(exc)`` treated the VIEW as missing. Live
Playwright e2e also landed on Databricks Sign-In / 401 because
``route.continue_()`` dropped ``extra_http_headers``.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/entity_search.py
   ``is_view_not_table_error`` / ``is_missing_relation_error`` also read
   ``exc.detail`` (SEA warehouse payload).
2. tests/e2e/conftest.py
   Re-apply ``Authorization: Bearer`` on every Playwright ``continue_``.
3. tests/units/graphdb/test_entity_search_sql.py
   SEA-detail classifier cases.
4. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_status_probe.py
   Zero-copy ``…_data`` VIEW still exists when SEA wraps the VIEW error.
5. tests/units/e2e/test_scenario_campaign_wiring.py
   Bearer headers are copied onto ``route.continue_``.

